dueDate.description:
This value specifies when the action is due. It's an optional string parameter that supports multiple formats including fixed dates, relative date expressions, and form tags.<br><br>
<details class="accordion-item">
  <summary class="accordion-header">See Examples</summary>
<br>
Examples:<br>
<pre>
{ "dueDate": "+7" }
{ "dueDate": "+7d" }
{ "dueDate": "+2w" }
{ "dueDate": "+1m" }
{ "dueDate": "+30d" }
{ "dueDate": "-7d" }
{ "dueDate": "+1BM" }
{ "dueDate": "+0EM" }
{ "dueDate": "last day of next quarter"}
{ "dueDate": "today"}
{ "dueDate": "tomorrow"}
{ "dueDate": "yesterday"}
{ "dueDate": "first day of this week}
{ "dueDate": "last day of next month}
{ "dueDate": "first day of next quarter}
{ "dueDate": "last day of this year}
{ "dueDate": "{Claim.IncidentDate}"}
</pre>
</details>

to.description:
Conditional (required when `sendEmail: true`). Defines the primary recipient email address(es) for the generated state form(s) when email distribution is enabled. Supports `{formTag}` resolution. To specify multiple recipients, separate each address with a comma.
```json
{
  "to": "wc.admin@company.com,{Claim.Adjuster.Email}"
}

